[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The whole library is one 48-line translation unit. Mechanically grepping
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c_src/src/driver.c` for *every* rejection construct:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```sh
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m grep -n 'return\|RETURN_ERROR\|assert\|NULL\|errno\|exit\|abort\|if *(\|switch\|#if\|else' \
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     c_src/src/driver.c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # -> no matches (outside of the copyright comment block)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Results, per construct:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | construct searched for | occurrences in `driver.c` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |------------------------|---------------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `return` (any)         | 0 (`driver` is `void`)    |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `return -1` / sentinel | 0                         |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `return NULL`          | 0                         |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `RETURN_ERROR`-style macro | 0                      |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `assert` / `static_assert` | 0                      |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | explicit range check (`if`, `<`, `>`, `?:`) | 0 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | null-pointer check     | 0 (no pointer parameters) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `switch` / `#ifdef` branch | 0 (only the header guard `DRIVER_H_`) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | error enum / status type | 0                       |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | min/max constant       | 0                         |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `errno` read or write  | 0                         |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `exit` / `abort`       | 0                         |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m So the library has **no explicit error surface**: `void driver(char c)` accepts
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m every one of the 256 `char` bit patterns, has no failure mode, no return value,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and no out-parameter. Its *entire* observable behaviour is the 14 lines it
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `printf`s to `stdout`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m That does not end the phase. The rows below are the rejection/edge conditions
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m that *do* exist for this API — the implicit ones at the language and FFI
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m boundary, i.e. every input that a real caller can construct and for which the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m two implementations could disagree. "Expected C result" is the ground truth the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rust must reproduce byte-for-byte; where the C does not reject at all, the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m required behaviour is *not rejecting in exactly the same way*.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1 | `driver` | `c == 0` (NUL, the C-string terminator / "empty" sentinel) | No rejection. 14 lines printed; classifiers report the raw `_IScntrl` bit, so `control: 2`, all other classes `0`; `to lower:`/`to upper:` emit a literal NUL byte (`%c` of `0`) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 2 | `driver` | `c == -1` i.e. `(char)0xFF`. Sign-extends to `-1`, which is the value of `EOF`; the ctype tables have a dedicated `EOF` slot at index `-1` | No rejection. All 12 classifiers `0`; `tolower(-1) == -1` and `toupper(-1) == -1`, and `printf("%c", -1)` writes the single byte `0xFF` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 3 | `driver` | `c == -128` i.e. `(char)0x80` — the most-negative `char`, the lowest legal index into glibc's ctype table | No rejection. Classifiers `0`; `tolower`/`toupper` return `128`, and `%c` of `128` writes the byte `0x80` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 4 | `driver` | any `c` in `-128..=-2` (high-bit set; `char` is **signed** on x86-64 Linux, so these index the ctype tables at a *negative* offset — out of the `0..=255` range the C standard defines for `isXXX`) | No rejection, no crash: glibc's tables are legally addressable from `-128`. Classifiers `0` for all of `-128..=-1`; `tolower`/`toupper` are the identity on `128..=254` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 5 | `driver` | `c == 127` (`DEL`) — one step past the last *printable* ASCII value and the largest positive `char` | No rejection. `control: 2`, everything else `0`; `%c` writes byte `0x7F` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 6 | `driver` | `c == 128` written by the caller as a wider integer (`128` is *not* representable in a signed `char`; implementation-defined narrowing) | No rejection. Narrows to `-128`, so output is identical to row 3 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 7 | `driver` | `c == 256`/`c == 0x100` passed as a wider integer — one step past the end of the `unsigned char` range | No rejection. Only the low 8 bits are consumed, so output is identical to `c == 0` (row 1) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 8 | `driver` | caller passes a full-width `int` with garbage in bits 8..31 (e.g. `0xDEADBE41`), the FFI analogue of an **out-of-range enum value**: the ABI passes sub-`int` args in a 32-bit register slot and the callee may not rely on the upper bits | No rejection. Callee sign-extends the low byte only (`movsbl`), so `0xDEADBE41` behaves exactly like `c == 'A'` (`0x41`) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 9 | `driver` | caller passes a negative wide `int` whose low byte is positive (e.g. `-65280 == 0xFFFF0100`) | No rejection. Low byte `0x00`, so identical to row 1 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 10 | `driver` | `c` is one of the values glibc classifies with *multiple* bits at once (`'0'..'9'` → `_ISalnum|_ISdigit|_ISxdigit|_ISgraph|_ISprint`) — the case where a normalising `0`/`1` translation would silently diverge | No rejection, and the returned `int` is the **raw masked bit**, not `1`: e.g. for `'0'`, `alphanumeric: 8`, `digit: 2048`, `hexadecimal: 4096`, `graphical: 32768`, `printing: 16384` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 11 | `driver` | `c == ' '` (0x20) — the one value that is `_ISblank|_ISspace|_ISprint` but **not** `_ISgraph` | No rejection. `space: 8192`, `blank: 1`, `printing: 16384`, `graphical: 0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 12 | `driver` | `c == '\t'` (0x09) — `_ISblank` **and** `_IScntrl` and `_ISspace` simultaneously | No rejection. `control: 2`, `space: 8192`, `blank: 1`; `printing: 0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 13 | `driver` | repeated invocation / locale already changed by an earlier caller (`driver` unconditionally calls `setlocale(LC_ALL, "C")` with no error check on its return value) | No rejection, and the return value of `setlocale` is discarded. Output is idempotent: the N-th call for a given `c` is byte-identical to the first |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 14 | `driver` | `stdout` redirected to a non-tty (fully buffered) and never flushed by the callee — `driver` calls no `fflush` | No rejection. The 14 lines sit in the `stdout` FILE buffer; both implementations must share the *same* libc `stdout` buffer, so a caller's `fflush(NULL)` drains both identically |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m No row is a real *rejection*, because the C rejects nothing — recording that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m truthfully is the point. Every row is exercised by a differential test in
