[38;5;252m[1m## Bugs found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The library is one function, [38;5;10mvoid driver(char c)[0m, which prints 12 [38;5;10m<ctype.h>[0m classifications plus [38;5;10mtolower[0m/[38;5;10mtoupper[0m of its argument. All 256 [38;5;10mchar[0m values matched on the happy path from the start — the bugs were only reachable through the configuration and error surfaces.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
1. [1mFrozen ctype tables.[22m The Rust had embedded a snapshot of glibc's [38;5;10m"C"[0m-locale tables. The C reads [38;5;10m(*__ctype_b_loc())[c][0m [3mlive[23m. Since [38;5;10mdriver[0m calls [38;5;10msetlocale(LC_ALL, "C")[0m — which sets the [1mglobal[22m locale and cannot displace one installed with [38;5;10muselocale()[0m — under a thread locale the C classifies through that locale instead. With [38;5;10mde_DE.ISO-8859-1[0m, byte [38;5;10m0x80[0m gave C [38;5;10mcontrol: 2[0m vs Rust [38;5;10m0[0m. Fixed by calling [38;5;10m__ctype_b_loc()[0m where the C macro does.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
2. [1mReimplemented case mapping.[22m Same root cause for [38;5;10mtolower[0m/[38;5;10mtoupper[0m: under [38;5;10mtr_TR[0m, glibc's [38;5;10mtolower('I')[0m is [38;5;10m'I'[0m (dotless [38;5;10mı[0m is not a single byte), but the Rust answered [38;5;10m'i'[0m. Fixed by calling libc.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
3. [1mSIGSEGV on an out-of-range argument.[22m [38;5;10mextern "C" fn driver(c: c_char)[0m makes rustc mark the parameter [38;5;10msignext[0m and emit [38;5;10mmovslq %edi[0m, using the [3mwhole[23m 32-bit register as the table index. GCC's code keeps only [38;5;10m%al[0m and re-reads it with [38;5;10mmovsbq[0m. Passing [38;5;10m0xDEAD_BE41[0m crashed the Rust where the C printed results for [38;5;10m'A'[0m. Fixed by taking [38;5;10mc_int[0m and narrowing explicitly; the exported symbol is unchanged and conforming callers see no difference.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Artifacts[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mSYMBOLS.md[0m, [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m (14 rows), [38;5;10mCONFIGS.md[0m (36 rows) in the crate root; suites in [38;5;10mtests/[0m ([38;5;10msmoke[0m, [38;5;10mconfigs[0m, [38;5;10merrors[0m, [38;5;10mlocale[0m) sharing [38;5;10mtests/common/mod.rs[0m, which loads [1mboth[22m [38;5;10m.so[0ms with [38;5;10mlibloading[0m and compares captured [38;5;10mstdout[0m byte-for-byte. Symbol diff is empty (C defines only [38;5;10mdriver[0m), and the Rust [38;5;10m.so[0m now imports the same [38;5;10m__ctype_b_loc[0m/[38;5;10mtolower[0m/[38;5;10mtoupper[0m/[38;5;10msetlocale[0m/[38;5;10mprintf[0m surface — which is what made the divergences fixable rather than merely hidden.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10m./build_and_test.sh[0m runs everything: 60 tests × 3 feature configurations × 2 profiles, all passing, with symbol parity re-checked per configuration.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## One caveat worth flagging[0m[0m
[0m[0m
My own suite initially had a blind spot, caught by [38;5;10mmutation_check.sh[0m: deleting [38;5;10msetlocale[0m from the Rust [3mpassed[23m, because [38;5;10mdiff_char[0m calls the C first and the C's own [38;5;10msetlocale[0m had already normalised the global locale before the Rust ran. I added [38;5;10mdiff_char_prepared[0m (re-establishes caller state before each side) and a direct [38;5;10msetlocale(LC_ALL, NULL)[0m side-effect assertion. All 12 mutants are now killed — including the three real bugs above, reintroduced as mutants.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two things I did not verify: behaviour on non-glibc libc or non-x86-64 targets (the [38;5;10m__ctype_b_loc[0m layout, signed [38;5;10mchar[0m, and the [38;5;10m%al[0m narrowing are all glibc/x86-64 specific), and [38;5;10mc_src[0m is not a git repo, so "unmodified" is attested by checksums of the three files rather than by version control.[0m[0m
